{"The blacklist check can be bypassed with case differences. Blacklisted emails are lowercased, but the incoming `guest` value is not lowercased before the `.includes(guest)` comparison. For example, `BAD@example.com` would not match `bad@example.com` in the blacklist.": 0.9918988943099976, "The permission check uses `&&` (AND) instead of `||` (OR), meaning a user must be both a team admin and a team owner to pass. The variable name `isTeamAdminOrOwner` indicates the intent was to allow either role. This effectively blocks team admins (who aren't owners) from adding guests.": 0.9963473677635193, "Notification emails are sent using the original `guests` input instead of the filtered `uniqueGuests`. This means emails may be sent to already-existing attendees or even blacklisted addresses that were intentionally excluded from being added.": 0.9957740902900696, "`uniqueGuests` does not deduplicate within the input array itself. If the caller provides the same email twice in the `guests` array, both will pass the filter and be created as separate attendee records.": 0.9636579751968384, "Hardcoded English string in Tooltip. The component already uses `useLocale()` and `t()` for other strings\u2014this tooltip should also be translated for i18n consistency.": 0.7236306071281433, "Using array index as `key` for a list where items can be removed from any position. When a middle email is deleted via `splice`, React will mismatch the remaining inputs, potentially showing stale values. Use a stable unique identifier.": 0.9322928786277771, "Missing `callToAction={null}` \u2014 the companion `OrganizerAddGuestsEmail` explicitly suppresses the call-to-action for this notification type. Attendees receiving a 'new guests added' notice likely don't need a CTA either.": 0.30172982811927795, "`sendAddGuestsEmails` does not respect `eventTypeMetadata` disable-email settings. Every other send function in this file gates on `eventTypeDisableHostEmail` / `eventTypeDisableAttendeeEmail`, but this function unconditionally sends to both host and attendees.": 0.9834280610084534, "`ZAddGuestsInputSchema` is a static Zod schema with no dependency on component state or props. Define it outside the component to avoid recreating it on every render.": 0.292436808347702, "`isInvalidEmail` is not reset to `false` in the `onSuccess` callback. If a user triggers validation error, then corrects the email and successfully submits, the error state persists. On reopening the dialog, the stale error message will be shown.": 0.9347007870674133, "`guests` should require at least one element. An empty array passes validation here but is always rejected by the handler, so failing early at schema level is preferable.": 0.13006345927715302, "`bookingId` should be constrained to positive integers. `z.number()` accepts floats and negative values, which are never valid booking IDs.": 0.27598682045936584, "`this.calEvent.attendees[0].name` will throw a `TypeError` if `attendees` is empty. Add a guard or use optional chaining with a fallback.": 0.7847514152526855, "Use `EMAIL_FROM_NAME` instead of `APP_NAME` for the email `from` field. The parent class and all other email templates use `EMAIL_FROM_NAME`, which respects the `process.env.EMAIL_FROM_NAME` override. Using `APP_NAME` directly ignores that customization.": 0.8762592077255249, "Pass `teamMember` into `renderEmail` so the template can render with the recipient's locale/timezone when the email is sent to a team member.": 0.6635262966156006}